<title>UK: Smiths half-year pretax profits up 15 pct.</title>
<headline>Smiths half-year pretax profits up 15 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to February 1</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		18.9		   vs 15.4</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 6.15		   vs 5.6</p>
<p> Pretax		     84.2		   vs 69.5</p>
<p> Turnover		   495.3		  vs 466.2</p>
<p> Operating result	 81.4		   vs 70.4</p>
<p> Exceptional gain	 4.0		    vs nil</p>
<p> Interest payable	 1.2		    vs 0.9</p>
<p>NOTE - Smiths Industries Plc said it made a first-half profit bfore tax and exceptionals of 80.2 million stg, compared to 69.5 million stg a year ago. The exceptional gain of 4.0 million stg was for a property sale.</p>
<p>Analysts had forecast pre-tax profits in a range between 76 and 84 million stg and an interim dividend of 6-6.2p.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
